# Villain Codex - Oracle Ascetic Mystery
SOURCELONG:Villain Codex	SOURCESHORT:VC	SOURCEDATE:2017-11

Ascetic Mysteries	KEY:Oracle ~ Ascetic Mystery	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:OracleClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.OracleMystery	DEFINE:AsceticMysteriesQualify|0	DESC:You have honed body and spirit through relentless discipline, drawing upon the divine mystery of the ascetic to grant your spells and powers.	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Ascetic Mystery ~ Final Revelation|PREMULT:2,[PRECLASS:1,Oracle=20],[PREVAREQ:Oracle_CF_FinalRevelation,0]	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|Ascetic Mysteries Class Skills|PREVAREQ:Oracle_CF_MysterySkills,0	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Ascetic Mystery Revelation|OracleMysteryLevel	BONUS:VAR|AsceticMysteriesQualify|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.104	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Oracle=1|Stone Fist|PREMULT:2,[PRECLASS:1,Oracle=2],[PREVAREQ:Oracle_CF_MysterySpell2,0]	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Oracle=2|Glide|PREMULT:2,[PRECLASS:1,Oracle=4],[PREVAREQ:Oracle_CF_MysterySpell4,0]	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Oracle=3|Force Punch|PREMULT:2,[PRECLASS:1,Oracle=6],[PREVAREQ:Oracle_CF_MysterySpell6,0]	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Oracle=4|Ethereal Fists|PREMULT:2,[PRECLASS:1,Oracle=8],[PREVAREQ:Oracle_CF_MysterySpell8,0]	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Oracle=5|Contact Other Plane|PREMULT:2,[PRECLASS:1,Oracle=10],[PREVAREQ:Oracle_CF_MysterySpell10,0]	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Oracle=6|Legend Lore|PREMULT:2,[PRECLASS:1,Oracle=12],[PREVAREQ:Oracle_CF_MysterySpell12,0]	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Oracle=7|Vision|PREMULT:2,[PRECLASS:1,Oracle=14],[PREVAREQ:Oracle_CF_MysterySpell14,0]	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Oracle=8|Frightful Aspect|PREMULT:2,[PRECLASS:1,Oracle=16],[PREVAREQ:Oracle_CF_MysterySpell16,0]	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Oracle=9|Iron Body|PREMULT:2,[PRECLASS:1,Oracle=18],[PREVAREQ:Oracle_CF_MysterySpell18,0]
Ascetic Mysteries Class Skills	CATEGORY:Internal	CSKILL:Acrobatics|Climb|Escape Artist|Swim

# --- Revelations
Absence of Body	KEY:Ascetic Mystery ~ Absence of Body	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:OracleClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.OracleRevelation.AsceticRevelation.Supernatural	DESC:You require half as much food and water to survive as a normal member of your race. Additionally, each time you hold your breath, you can do so for an additional number of rounds equal to your oracle level. At 15th level, you no longer need to eat or drink and can hold your breath for 10 times as long (2 minutes per point of Constitution, plus 1 additional minute per oracle level).	SOURCEPAGE:p.104
Absence of Form	KEY:Ascetic Mystery ~ Absence of Form	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:OracleClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.OracleRevelation.AsceticRevelation.SpellLike	DEFINE:AsceticAbsenceOfFormRounds|0	DESC:You gain feather fall as a spell-like ability, which you can use a number of rounds per day equal to your oracle level. The rounds do not need to be used consecutively. If you are in mid fall when this ability's duration expires, you take falling damage as if you fell from the altitude you were at when the spell ended. At 10th level, you can also apply your daily rounds of this ability to use air walk.	BONUS:VAR|AsceticAbsenceOfFormRounds|classlevel("Oracle")	SPELLS:Ascetic Absence of Form|TIMES=AsceticAbsenceOfFormRounds|CASTERLEVEL=classlevel("Oracle")|Feather Fall	SPELLS:Ascetic Absence of Form|TIMES=AsceticAbsenceOfFormRounds|CASTERLEVEL=classlevel("Oracle")|Air Walk|PRECLASS:1,Oracle=10	SOURCEPAGE:p.104
Ascetic Armor	KEY:Ascetic Mystery ~ Ascetic Armor	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:OracleClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.OracleRevelation.AsceticRevelation.Supernatural	DEFINE:AsceticArmorBonus|0	DEFINE:AsceticArmorLVL|0	DEFINE:AsceticArmorHasArmor|0	DEFINE:AsceticArmorEncumbered|0	DEFINE:AsceticArmorRestricted|0	DESC:You can use meditative techniques that temporarily cause attacks to bounce off your skin, as long as you aren't wearing armor or carrying a medium or heavy load. These techniques grant you a +%1 armor bonus to AC. At 7th level, and every 4 levels thereafter, this bonus increases by 2. At 13th level, the techniques also grant DR 5/unarmed strikes or natural attacks. You can gain the benefits of ascetic armor for 1 hour per day per oracle level. The hours do not need to be consecutive, but you must spend them in 1-hour increments.|AsceticArmorBonus	BONUS:VAR|AsceticArmorLVL|classlevel("Oracle")|TYPE=Level	BONUS:VAR|AsceticArmorHasArmor|1|PREVARGTEQ:var("COUNT[EQTYPE.ARMOR.EQUIPPED]"),1	BONUS:VAR|AsceticArmorEncumbered|1|PREVARGTEQ:ENCUMBERANCE,1	BONUS:VAR|AsceticArmorRestricted|AsceticArmorHasArmor+AsceticArmorEncumbered|TYPE=Boolean	BONUS:VAR|AsceticArmorBonus|4+2*min(4,max(0,(AsceticArmorLVL-3)/4))	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|AsceticArmorBonus|TYPE=Armor|PREVAREQ:AsceticArmorRestricted,0	SOURCEPAGE:p.104
Fleet	KEY:Ascetic Mystery ~ Fleet	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:OracleClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.OracleRevelation.AsceticRevelation.Extraordinary	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Oracle ~ Lame	DEFINE:AsceticFleetBonus|0	DESC:You gain a +%1-foot enhancement bonus to your base land speed. You lose this extra speed if you wear any armor or carry a medium or heavy load. At 7th level, and every 6 levels thereafter, this bonus increases by 10 feet.|AsceticFleetBonus	BONUS:VAR|AsceticFleetBonus|10+10*min(3,max(0,(classlevel("Oracle")-1)/6))	BONUS:MOVEADD|TYPE=Walk|AsceticFleetBonus|PREVARLT:ENCUMBERANCE,1,var("COUNT[EQTYPE.ARMOR.EQUIPPED]"),1	SOURCEPAGE:p.104
Martial Disciple	KEY:Ascetic Mystery ~ Martial Disciple	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:OracleClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.OracleRevelation.AsceticRevelation.Supernatural	DESC:Through meditation and study of monastic forms of combat, you have learned a lethal form of unarmed combat. You gain Improved Unarmed Strike as a bonus feat, even if you do not meet the prerequisites. You gain the unarmed strike damage of a monk of your oracle level. If you also have monk levels, those levels stack for the purpose of determining your unarmed strike damage.	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Improved Unarmed Strike	BONUS:UDAM|CLASS.Monk|classlevel("Oracle")	SOURCEPAGE:p.104
Oracular Spellstrike	KEY:Ascetic Mystery ~ Oracular Spellstrike	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:OracleClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.OracleRevelation.AsceticRevelation.Supernatural	PRECLASS:1,Oracle=7	DESC:By harnessing a synergy of unarmed combat and spellcasting, you have uncovered a means of channeling spell energy quickly through your unarmed strikes. This resembles the magus spellstrike ability, except it works with unarmed strikes only, no matter what other abilities you have. Additionally, it uses spells from the cleric spell list, not the magus spell list. You must be at least 7th level before selecting this revelation.	SOURCEPAGE:p.104
Rapid Convalescence	KEY:Ascetic Mystery ~ Rapid Convalescence	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:OracleClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.OracleRevelation.AsceticRevelation.Supernatural	DESC:You reduce the number of consecutive successful saves needed to recover from a disease or poison by 1 (to a minimum of 1). Additionally, you can sacrifice one of your unused spell slots for the day to gain an enhancement bonus equal to that spell slot's level on your next save to resist the effects of poison or disease, provided the save is attempted within 1 minute per level of spell expended.	SOURCEPAGE:p.104
Spell Deflection	KEY:Ascetic Mystery ~ Spell Deflection	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:OracleClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.OracleRevelation.AsceticRevelation.Supernatural	PRECLASS:1,Oracle=11	DESC:You can use a readied action to counterspell any spell being cast on you or an adjacent ally that requires a ranged touch attack (such as a ray). In order to successfully counter the spell, you must make an unarmed attack roll. If the result of this attack roll is higher than 20 + the spell's caster level, the spell is negated with no effect. At 17th level, any spell you successfully negate is reflected back at the caster with the same ranged touch attack result. You must be at least 11th level before selecting this revelation.	SOURCEPAGE:p.104

# --- Final Revelation (no official version; PFS clarification grants the monk's Perfect Self)
Final Revelation	KEY:Ascetic Mystery ~ Final Revelation	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:OracleClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.FinalRevelation	DESC:You have become a magical creature. You are forevermore treated as an outsider rather than as a humanoid (or whatever your creature type was) for the purpose of spells and magical effects. Additionally, you gain damage reduction 10/chaotic, which allows you to ignore the first 10 points of damage from any attack made by a nonchaotic weapon or by any natural attack made by a creature that doesn't have similar damage reduction. Unlike other outsiders, you can still be brought back from the dead as if you were a member of your previous creature type. (No Final Revelation exists as printed for the Ascetic mystery; per the Pathfinder Society Campaign Clarifications this mystery grants the monk's Perfect Self ability. This is not official errata.)	DR:10/Chaotic	SOURCEPAGE:p.104

# Villain Codex - Barbarian Rage Powers (Atavism Totem line, Nature's Scourge pp.140)
Atavism Totem, Lesser	KEY:Rage Power ~ Atavism Totem (Lesser)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ClassFeatures.BarbarianClassFeatures.RagePower.SpecialQuality.Supernatural	DESC:The barbarian gains a bite attack; if she already has a bite attack, it deals damage as if the barbarian were one size larger. This is a totem rage power.	SOURCEPAGE:p.140	ASPECT:ChildAbility|Rage
Atavism Totem	KEY:Rage Power ~ Atavism Totem	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ClassFeatures.BarbarianClassFeatures.RagePower.SpecialQuality.Supernatural	PREVARGTEQ:RagePowersLVL,6	DESC:The barbarian gains ferocity. This is a totem rage power. The barbarian must be at least 6th level to select this rage power.	SOURCEPAGE:p.140	ASPECT:ChildAbility|Rage
Atavism Totem, Greater	KEY:Rage Power ~ Atavism Totem (Greater)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ClassFeatures.BarbarianClassFeatures.RagePower.SpecialQuality.Supernatural	PREVARGTEQ:RagePowersLVL,10	DESC:The barbarian gains trample. This is a totem rage power. The barbarian must be at least 10th level to select this rage power.	SOURCEPAGE:p.140	ASPECT:ChildAbility|Rage

# Villain Codex - Barbarian Rage Powers (Savage Marauders pp.176)
Erratic Charge	KEY:Rage Power ~ Erratic Charge	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ClassFeatures.BarbarianClassFeatures.RagePower.SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:As part of the full-round action to perform a charge attack against a creature at least 20 feet away, the barbarian can move 5 feet in any direction before making the charge. This movement is not a 5-foot step and provokes attacks of opportunity as normal, and using this option reduces the maximum distance of the charge by 10 feet.	SOURCEPAGE:p.176	ASPECT:ChildAbility|Rage
Erratic Charge, Greater	KEY:Rage Power ~ Erratic Charge (Greater)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ClassFeatures.BarbarianClassFeatures.RagePower.SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Rage Power ~ Erratic Charge	PREVARGTEQ:RagePowersLVL,8	DESC:The barbarian can move 10 feet when using erratic charge. If she does so, the creature she is charging must be at least 20 feet away and the movement reduces the maximum distance of her charge by 20 feet. The barbarian must have the erratic charge rage power and be at least 8th level to select this rage power.	SOURCEPAGE:p.176	ASPECT:ChildAbility|Rage
Furious Draw	KEY:Rage Power ~ Furious Draw	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ClassFeatures.BarbarianClassFeatures.RagePower.SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:The barbarian is treated as having the Quick Draw feat.	SOURCEPAGE:p.176	ASPECT:ChildAbility|Rage
Furious Barrage	KEY:Rage Power ~ Furious Barrage	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ClassFeatures.BarbarianClassFeatures.RagePower.SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Rage Power ~ Furious Draw	PREVARGTEQ:RagePowersLVL,4	DESC:The barbarian is treated as having the Rapid Shot feat, but only for the purpose of attacking with thrown weapons. She need not meet the feat's prerequisites. The barbarian must have the furious draw rage power and be at least 4th level to select this rage power.	SOURCEPAGE:p.176	ASPECT:ChildAbility|Rage
Savage Hurl	KEY:Rage Power ~ Savage Hurl	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ClassFeatures.BarbarianClassFeatures.RagePower.SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:The barbarian gains a +1 bonus on ranged attack rolls with thrown weapons that add her Dexterity bonus to the attack roll. This bonus increases to +2 at 4th level if the barbarian's Strength modifier is at least +4, to +3 at 8th level if her Strength modifier is at least +6, and to +4 at 12th level if her Strength modifier is at least +8.	SOURCEPAGE:p.176	ASPECT:ChildAbility|Rage
Two-Fanged Pounce	KEY:Rage Power ~ Two-Fanged Pounce	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ClassFeatures.BarbarianClassFeatures.RagePower.SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	DESC:If the barbarian is wielding a pair of daggers, kukris, or punching daggers, she can attack once with each of the two weapons when she charges. If she does, she loses the bonus on attack rolls for charging and takes an additional -2 penalty to her AC, and she applies precision damage or effects that occur on a hit only once, even if she hits with both attacks.	SOURCEPAGE:p.176	ASPECT:ChildAbility|Rage

# Villain Codex - Cavalier Order (Brutal Slavers p.20)
Order of the Whip	KEY:Cavalier Order ~ Order of the Whip	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:CavalierClassFeatures.CavalierOrder.SpecialQuality	DESC:Order of the whip cavaliers seek to dominate the weak through pain and fear. Edicts: The cavalier must seek out those weaker than himself to punish and torture, force others to obey his commands without question, and strive to cause pain and suffering wherever possible. Since these edicts are evil, he must be of an evil alignment. Challenge: Whenever an order of the whip cavalier issues a challenge, he receives a +1 morale bonus on all melee damage rolls against the target of his challenge as long as he damaged the creature in the previous round. This bonus increases by +1 for every 4 levels the cavalier has (to a maximum of +5 at 17th level). Skills: An order of the whip cavalier adds Knowledge (local) and Knowledge (nobility) to his list of class skills. Whenever he uses Intimidate to force another creature to do what he says, he receives a bonus on the check equal to 1/2 his cavalier level (minimum +1). Whip Crack (Ex, 2nd level): The cavalier becomes proficient with a whip and gains Whip Mastery as a bonus feat. When a creature whose number of Hit Dice is less than or equal to 1/2 the cavalier's level takes nonlethal damage from the cavalier's whip, it is shaken for 1 round. This does not stack with other fear effects. Inspiring Pain (Ex, 8th level): As a swift action, the cavalier can allow allies within 30 feet to deal nonlethal damage with their weapons without taking the usual -4 penalty (the weapon must still be capable of dealing nonlethal damage). Affected allies gain a +2 bonus on nonlethal weapon damage rolls. This effect lasts for 1 round and can be used once every 5 minutes. Assert Authority (Ex, 15th level): Whenever an enemy makes a melee attack against the cavalier or one of his adjacent slaves or servants, that enemy provokes an attack of opportunity from the cavalier, and the cavalier gains a +2 morale bonus on this attack of opportunity. If the enemy's attack was a confirmed critical hit, the cavalier counts the enemy as if it were the target of his challenge for this attack of opportunity.	CSKILL:Knowledge (Local)|Knowledge (Nobility)	SOURCEPAGE:p.20

# Villain Codex - Oracle Curse (Fang Monastery p.104)
Toxic Blood	KEY:Oracle ~ Toxic Blood	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:OracleClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.OracleCurse	DESC:Your body is ravaged by a potent, slow-acting poison that resists all treatment. Whenever you must attempt a Fortitude save to resist a poison effect, roll twice and take the lowest result. Additionally, you need one more consecutive successful save to end an ongoing poison. You lose any immunity to poison you have upon receiving this curse, and you become immune to delay poison and neutralize poison, as well as other attempts to suppress or remove the poison from which you are suffering. You gain the poison use ability. At 5th level, you are so envenomed that your touch becomes poisonous. Once per day for every 4 oracle levels you have, you can deliver a unique contact poison as a touch attack or via an unarmed strike or natural weapon. This poison deals 1d2 points of Dexterity damage per round for 5 rounds. Poisoned creatures can attempt a Fortitude save (DC = 10 + 1/2 your oracle level + your Charisma modifier) each round; success negates the damage and ends the affliction. At 10th level, the poison deals 1d3 points of Dexterity damage per round for 7 rounds. At 15th level, you can expend a use of your poison touch to transfer any poison effect you are currently experiencing from yourself to another creature. The touched creature must immediately attempt a saving throw against the poison (using the poison's initial DC and duration for a single dose, regardless of how many doses are currently affecting you). If the creature fails its save, the poison ceases to act on you, as if you had succeeded at all the necessary saves (this bypasses your immunity to effects that remove poison).	SOURCEPAGE:p.104

# Villain Codex - Alchemist Discoveries (Thieves' Guild p.236)
Incendiary Charge	KEY:Discovery ~ Incendiary Charge	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:AlchemistClassFeatures.SpecialAttack.AlchemistDiscovery.AlchemistBombModifier	PREVARGTEQ:DiscoveryQualifyLVL,4	DESC:An incendiary charge is a bomb specifically designed to overcome the effects of any nonmagical object's hardness. As a full-round action, the alchemist can place an incendiary charge that burns and eats away at an object, dealing normal bomb damage to it. (The damage is not halved against an object with hardness, unlike most energy damage.) Furthermore, the incendiary charge ignores the first 5 points of hardness of the material being damaged. This discovery does not stack with other discoveries that modify bombs. The alchemist must be at least 4th level before selecting this discovery.	SOURCEPAGE:p.236
Penetrating Charge	KEY:Discovery ~ Penetrating Charge	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:AlchemistClassFeatures.SpecialAttack.AlchemistDiscovery.AlchemistBombModifier	DESC:A penetrating charge is a bomb specifically designed to disable locks and similar mechanisms, though not other means of sealing a door, a container, or other sorts of devices. As a full-round action, the alchemist can place a penetrating charge on a lock. Instead of dealing damage, the penetrating charge seeps into the mechanism and eats away at it, granting a +5 circumstance bonus on any subsequent Disable Device checks against the mechanism. A creature can spend 10 minutes and attempt an appropriate Craft check (DC 15) to fix the lock and remove this bonus. This discovery does not stack with other discoveries that modify bombs.	SOURCEPAGE:p.236

Pallid Vector Traits	KEY:Pallid Vector Traits	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Template.Supernatural	VISIBLE:DISPLAY	DESC:This creature is treated as undead for the purposes of negative and positive energy, and it gains immunity to disease, exhaustion, fatigue, poison, and stunning. It gains stench (10 rounds) and a Constitution-based pallid gift disease on all melee attacks (Fort save; 1d6 Con and 1d6 Wis damage plus fatigue; ability damage cannot be healed and fatigue cannot be removed while infected; cure 2 consecutive saves). Pale Rebirth (Su): when the creature dies it rises as a plague zombie 1 round later (a humanoid instead rises as a more powerful undead by Hit Dice: 1-3 plague zombie, 4-5 ghast, 6-7 wight, 8+ vampire); sprinkling holy water on the body before it rises prevents this.	SOURCEPAGE:p.68

Fortune-Teller	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:VillainCodexArchetype.BardArchetype	DESC:Bard archetype (Carnival Troupe). Instead of song and dance, a fortune-teller influences people by divining their fate. Fortune-Teller's Divinations alters the bard spell list. Oracular Performance (1st) alters bardic performance and replaces countersong and distraction. Fortune-Teller's Acumen (2nd) replaces well-versed. Transparent Fate (8th) replaces dirge of doom.	SOURCEPAGE:p.32
Oracular Performance	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:BardClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.Supernatural	PRECLASS:1,Bard=1	DESC:A fortune-teller can use Perform (oratory) to read a fortune as part of a bardic performance. Once per hour when the bard performs a fortune-telling using a fortune-teller's deck, a crystal ball, or a similar item, he can read the fortune of one subject of the bardic performance, as part of the same action used to activate the performance. He rolls d%, adds his bard level, and consults the oracular performance table. The outcome depends on whether the chosen creature is an ally (beneficial performance) or an enemy (detrimental performance). Ally: 1-35 woe, 36-65 inconclusive, 66+ weal. Enemy: 1-35 weal, 36-65 inconclusive, 66+ woe. On an inconclusive result the reading yields nothing and the subject is affected normally. For an ally, a weal result increases the subject's numeric bonus from the performance by 1 and a woe result decreases it by 1 (minimum 0); only numeric bonuses are affected. For an enemy, a weal result grants a +2 bonus on its save to negate the performance and a woe result imposes a -2 penalty; this has no effect if the performance requires no save. Adjustments on a foe last only for that instance of the performance; adjustments on an ally last 1 minute. This alters bardic performance and replaces countersong and distraction.	SOURCEPAGE:p.32
Fortune-Teller's Acumen	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:BardClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	PRECLASS:1,Bard=2	DESC:At 2nd level, whenever he casts a spell from the divination school, a fortune-teller can use a fortune-teller's deck, crystal ball, or similar item instead of the spell's material component, as long as the cost of the material component is no more than 100 gp per bard level. If he casts the spell using such an item and the spell's normal material component (regardless of that component's cost), he casts the spell at +1 caster level. This special focus can't be used with other special foci that have a similar effect, but can be used with spells that normally require a focus component (which must also be provided). This replaces well-versed.	SOURCEPAGE:p.32
Transparent Fate	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:BardClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.Supernatural	PRECLASS:1,Bard=8	DESC:At 8th level, the fortune-teller can cause all enemies within 30 feet to have their near future revealed for all to see. A successful Will save (DC = 10 + 1/2 the fortune-teller's level + his Charisma modifier) negates the effect. Any creature attacked by an affected enemy gains a +2 bonus to AC and on saving throws against the attack. As a secondary effect, if an affected creature's hit points are reduced to less than its Constitution score, it also sees a vision of its own death and must succeed at another Will save or become frightened for 1 round (a given creature saves against this secondary effect at most once per performance). A creature targeted by oracular performance when this performance began applies any save DC adjustment to this secondary save as well. This bardic performance replaces dirge of doom.	SOURCEPAGE:p.32
Hellcat	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:VillainCodexArchetype.MonkArchetype	DESC:Monk archetype (Diabolical Church). A hellcat must be lawful evil or lawful neutral, altering the monk's alignment requirements, class skills (gains Knowledge [planes] and Survival, loses Craft, Knowledge [history], Perform, and Profession), weapon proficiencies, and bonus feat list. Hellcat Fury (1st) replaces stunning fist and fast movement. Torture Training (2nd) replaces evasion, purity of body, and improved evasion. Crucible of Pain (3rd) replaces slow fall and still mind. Hellcat Ki (4th) alters the ki pool and replaces wholeness of body and diamond body.	SOURCEPAGE:p.92
Hellcat Fury	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MonkClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	PRECLASS:1,Monk=1	DESC:At 1st level, a hellcat can deal slashing damage with his unarmed strikes. At 4th level, whenever he confirms a critical hit with his slashing unarmed strike, the target also takes 1d4 points of bleed damage. The bleed damage increases to 1d6 at 8th level, 1d8 at 12th, 1d10 at 16th, and 1d12 at 20th. This replaces stunning fist and fast movement.	SOURCEPAGE:p.92
Torture Training	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MonkClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	PRECLASS:1,Monk=2	DESC:At 2nd level, a hellcat who fails a save against an effect that causes him to become fatigued, sickened, or staggered can attempt a second save against the effect at the end of his next turn (only one additional save is allowed). At 5th level, he can also attempt this second save against effects that would cause him to become frightened or shaken. At 9th level, he can also attempt it against effects that would cause him to become exhausted, nauseated, or dazed. This replaces evasion, purity of body, and improved evasion.	SOURCEPAGE:p.92
Crucible of Pain	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MonkClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	PRECLASS:1,Monk=3	DESC:At 3rd level, a hellcat gains an amount of DR/-- equal to half his monk level against nonlethal damage. In addition, he is inured to hot climate effects as if using endure elements. This replaces slow fall and still mind.	SOURCEPAGE:p.92
Hellcat Ki	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MonkClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.Supernatural	PRECLASS:1,Monk=4	DESC:At 4th level, a hellcat gains a pool of ki points usable as per the monk class feature, with the following additions. Besides spending ki to gain an extra attack, increased speed, or improved AC, a hellcat can spend 1 ki point as a swift action to enhance his sight (60-foot darkvision) or his sense of smell (the scent ability) for 1 minute per level. At 7th level, he can spend 1 ki point as a swift action to gain fire resistance 5 for 1 round per level (10 at 10th level, 15 at 14th). At 11th level, he can spend 1 ki point as a swift action to become silhouetted with a ghostly flame for 1 round per level, making him harder to see in light but easier to see in darkness: invisible in bright light, concealment (20% miss chance) in normal light, no benefit in dim light, and giving off candlelight in darkness so creatures can see him even without darkvision. If he takes an action that would break invisibility while in bright light, his invisibility is reduced to concealment until the end of his next turn. This alters the ki pool and replaces wholeness of body and diamond body.	SOURCEPAGE:p.92
Hunting Serpent	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:VillainCodexArchetype.NinjaArchetype	DESC:Ninja archetype (Fang Monastery). A hunting serpent gains Survival as a class skill but loses Knowledge (nobility), altering class skills. Relentless Pursuit (3rd) replaces no trace. Death Mark (4th) replaces uncanny dodge, improved uncanny dodge, and the ninja tricks gained at 12th and 16th levels. Certain Demise (10th) replaces the ninja trick gained at 10th level.	SOURCEPAGE:p.105
Relentless Pursuit	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:NinjaClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	PRECLASS:1,Ninja=3	DESC:At 3rd level, a hunting serpent gains a +1 bonus on Diplomacy checks to gather information and on Survival checks to identify or follow tracks. The bonus increases by 1 for every 3 ninja levels beyond 3rd. This replaces no trace.	SOURCEPAGE:p.105
Death Mark	KEY:Ninja ~ Death Mark	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:NinjaClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	PRECLASS:1,Ninja=4	DESC:At 4th level, as a swift action once per day, a hunting serpent can mark an opponent damaged by her sneak attack for death. She gains a +1 competence bonus on attack and damage rolls against an opponent affected by death mark, as well as on Survival checks to track the marked creature. The bonuses and the number of uses per day increase by 1 at 8th, 12th, and 16th levels. The effects last 24 hours, until the marked creature is slain, or until she marks another creature, whichever comes first. This replaces uncanny dodge, improved uncanny dodge, and the ninja tricks gained at 12th and 16th levels.	SOURCEPAGE:p.105
Certain Demise	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:NinjaClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	PRECLASS:1,Ninja=10	DESC:At 10th level, the hunting serpent's sneak attack damage applies on the first attack she makes each round against the target of her death mark ability, even if it normally wouldn't. Other effects that trigger on a sneak attack do not apply with this ability. This replaces the ninja trick gained at 10th level.	SOURCEPAGE:p.105
Mirror Witch	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:VillainCodexArchetype.WitchArchetype	DESC:Witch archetype (Regal Court). Patron Mirror (1st) replaces the witch's familiar and the familiar abilities table; a mirror witch draws on the latent magic of a mirror as a conduit to her patron instead of a living familiar. The patron mirror grants a +2 bonus on Diplomacy checks and gains new powers as the witch levels: cryptic omens and seek guidance (1st), greater omens (3rd), specialized knowledge (5th), clairvoyance/clairaudience (7th), scrying (11th), and mirror casting (13th).	SOURCEPAGE:p.152
Patron Mirror	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:WitchClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.Supernatural	PRECLASS:1,Witch=1	DESC:At 1st level, a mirror witch creates a direct link to the power of her patron. She chooses a patron as normal, but instead of gaining a familiar as the conduit to her patron, she uses a mirror (worth at least 10 gp) to speak to a fragment of her patron's power that teaches her magic and acts as a counselor. The mirror is essentially an immobile familiar. She activates it with a minute-long ritual that calls the patron fragment to manifest through the mirror; while the connection is open she can prepare spells, add new spells to the mirror, and use the mirror's special abilities. In place of an ordinary familiar's boost, the mirror grants a +2 bonus on Diplomacy checks whether or not the mirror is nearby. The mirror can't be used for abilities that require the presence of a familiar, such as the blight hex. If destroyed, it can be replaced 1 day later by attuning a new suitable mirror at a cost of 500 gp per witch level via an 8-hour ritual, losing spells stored in the previous mirror as normal for a lost familiar. As the witch gains levels the mirror's hardness, hit points, and Intelligence increase per the Patron Mirror table. This replaces the witch's familiar.	BONUS:SKILL|Diplomacy|2	SOURCEPAGE:p.152
Cryptic Omens	KEY:Witch ~ Cryptic Omens	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:WitchClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	PRECLASS:1,Witch=1	DESC:Each day, when a mirror witch consults with her patron mirror, the fragment speaks a few words of cryptic advice about her future that make sense at just the right moment. Once per day, after receiving this advice, she can gain one of the following without taking an action: a +2 insight bonus on a saving throw she is about to attempt; a +2 insight bonus on a Bluff, Diplomacy, or Sense Motive check she is about to attempt; or, instead of rolling initiative, treat her initiative as if she rolled a 12 (she can't use this last option if she can't act during a surprise round). She doesn't choose the benefit while consulting the mirror, but when she would roll the save, initiative, or skill check.	SOURCEPAGE:p.152
Seek Guidance	KEY:Witch ~ Seek Guidance	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:WitchClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	PRECLASS:1,Witch=1	DESC:Whenever the mirror witch consults with her patron fragment, she can spend 10 minutes instead of the usual 1 minute and attempt a single Knowledge check, gaining a +2 insight bonus on that check.	SOURCEPAGE:p.152
Greater Omens	KEY:Witch ~ Greater Omens	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:WitchClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	PRECLASS:1,Witch=3	DESC:The number of times per day the mirror witch can use cryptic omens increases by the Intelligence modifier of the patron mirror. In addition, after consulting with her patron for 1 minute, she can expend a use of cryptic omens to gain the effects of augury instead of one of the usual three benefits.	SOURCEPAGE:p.152
Specialized Knowledge	KEY:Witch ~ Specialized Knowledge	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:WitchClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	PRECLASS:1,Witch=5	DESC:The mirror witch chooses a number of Knowledge skills equal to the patron mirror's Intelligence modifier (and chooses more as that modifier increases). When she consults her patron fragment with seek guidance for a chosen Knowledge skill, the insight bonus increases by an amount equal to the mirror's Intelligence modifier (for example, +4 instead of +2 at 5th-6th level).	SOURCEPAGE:p.152
Clairvoyance/Clairaudience	KEY:Witch ~ Clairvoyance-Clairaudience	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:WitchClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.SpellLike	PRECLASS:1,Witch=7	DESC:By consulting her patron fragment for 10 minutes, the mirror witch can expend a single use of cryptic omens to cast clairvoyance/clairaudience as a spell-like ability with a caster level equal to her witch level.	SOURCEPAGE:p.153
Scrying	KEY:Witch ~ Scrying	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:WitchClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.SpellLike	PRECLASS:1,Witch=11	DESC:By consulting with her patron fragment for 1 hour, the mirror witch can expend a single use of cryptic omens to use scrying as a spell-like ability with a caster level equal to her witch level, using the patron mirror as the focus.	SOURCEPAGE:p.153
Mirror Casting	KEY:Witch ~ Mirror Casting	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:WitchClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.Supernatural	PRECLASS:1,Witch=13	DESC:When using the mirror's scrying ability, detect chaos, detect evil, detect good, detect law, detect magic, message, read magic, and tongues all function reliably through the sensor. Also, if the mirror witch is at least 15th level, there is a 5% chance each of the following spells operates successfully through the sensor: cause fear, charm person, command, crushing despair, deep slumber, enthrall, fear, hold person, moonstruck [APG], seek thoughts, and sleep; a creature that succeeds at its save against one of these linked spells is forever immune to that particular mirror witch's attempts to cast that spell on it through her mirror.	SOURCEPAGE:p.153
Seasoned Commander	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:VillainCodexArchetype.FighterArchetype	DESC:Fighter archetype (Ruthless Brigands). Strategic Training alters skill ranks per level and class skills and replaces the 1st-level bonus combat feat and proficiency with heavy armor and tower shields. Tactician (3rd) replaces armor training 1. Inspiring Speech (5th) replaces weapon training 1 and 3. Inspire Greatness (9th) replaces weapon training 2. Greater Tactician (11th) replaces armor training 3. Inspire Heroics (15th) replaces armor training 4. Master Tactician (17th) replaces weapon training 4. Armor training 2 is retained.	SOURCEPAGE:p.164
Strategic Training	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:FighterClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	PRECLASS:1,Fighter=1	DESC:A seasoned commander gains 4 skill ranks + a number of skill ranks equal to his Intelligence modifier at each level instead of the normal 2 skill ranks + Intelligence modifier, and adds Diplomacy, Knowledge (geography), Knowledge (nobility), Linguistics, and Sense Motive to his list of class skills. This alters skill ranks per level and class skills and replaces the 1st-level bonus fighter combat feat and proficiency with heavy armor and tower shields.	SOURCEPAGE:p.164
Tactician	KEY:Fighter ~ Tactician	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:FighterClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	PRECLASS:1,Fighter=3	DESC:At 3rd level, a seasoned commander gains the cavalier's tactician class feature, treating his fighter level as his cavalier level for the purpose of this ability. This replaces armor training 1.	SOURCEPAGE:p.164
Inspiring Speech	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:FighterClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	PRECLASS:1,Fighter=5	DESC:At 5th level, a seasoned commander can give an inspiring speech as a standard action once per day. All allies who can hear the speech gain the benefits of inspire courage, granting bonuses 1 lower than those granted by a bard of the seasoned commander's fighter level, lasting 1 round per fighter level + his Charisma modifier (abilities that affect a bardic performance, such as Lingering Performance, have no effect on this ability). At 7th level he can perform the speech as a move action, and at 13th level as a swift action. This replaces weapon training 1 and 3.	SOURCEPAGE:p.164
Inspire Greatness	KEY:Fighter ~ Inspire Greatness	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:FighterClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	PRECLASS:1,Fighter=9	DESC:At 9th level, a seasoned commander gains an additional daily use of his inspiring speech ability, and he can also choose to use his inspiring speech to grant the effects of inspire greatness to one ally (instead of inspire courage). For every 2 levels beyond 9th he can target one additional ally while using this ability (up to a maximum of six at 19th level). This otherwise functions like the seasoned commander's inspire courage ability. If he uses an inspiring speech before the duration of the previous one ends, the new speech replaces the old. This replaces weapon training 2.	SOURCEPAGE:p.164
Greater Tactician	KEY:Fighter ~ Greater Tactician	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:FighterClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	PRECLASS:1,Fighter=11	DESC:At 11th level, the seasoned commander gains the cavalier's greater tactician class feature, treating his fighter level as his cavalier level for the purpose of this ability. This replaces armor training 3.	SOURCEPAGE:p.164
Inspire Heroics	KEY:Fighter ~ Inspire Heroics	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:FighterClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	PRECLASS:1,Fighter=15	DESC:At 15th level, a seasoned commander gains an additional daily use of his inspiring speech, and he can also choose to use his inspiring speech to grant the effects of inspire heroics to one ally (instead of inspire courage or inspire greatness). For every 2 levels beyond 15th he can target one additional ally while using this ability. This otherwise functions like the seasoned commander's inspire courage ability. This replaces armor training 4.	SOURCEPAGE:p.164
Master Tactician	KEY:Fighter ~ Master Tactician	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:FighterClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	PRECLASS:1,Fighter=17	DESC:At 17th level, the seasoned commander gains the cavalier's master tactician class feature, treating his fighter level as his cavalier level for the purpose of this ability. This replaces weapon training 4.	SOURCEPAGE:p.164
Voice of the Void	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:VillainCodexArchetype.MediumArchetype	DESC:Medium archetype (Sinister Cult). Emissary alters spirit: the medium channels alien emissaries, and for each point of influence an emissary gains he takes a -1 penalty on Will saves, Wisdom checks, and Wisdom-based skill checks (and takes 2d4 Wisdom damage on awakening if controlled). Surge of the Void (1st) modifies spirit surge. Blasphemy (1st) alters taboo. Void Channeler (3rd) replaces haunt channeler.	SOURCEPAGE:p.212
Surge of the Void	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MediumClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.Supernatural	PRECLASS:1,Medium=1	DESC:The voice of the void can use spirit surge additional times per day without incurring influence, but each time he does he is confused for 1 round. If this confusion would cause him to babble, he can instead act normally, but his emissary gains 1 point of influence over him. He can't use this ability if he is immune to confusion, but he can remove the confused condition when affected by it. This temporary confusion clearly indicates he isn't fully in control, so using this power on a Diplomacy check in a negotiation, for example, might prejudice the other party against him regardless of his check result. This modifies spirit surge.	SOURCEPAGE:p.212
Blasphemy	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MediumClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	PRECLASS:1,Medium=1	DESC:Emissaries demand that a medium perform acts appealing to their alien whims. These work just like taboos for an ordinary medium, but in addition to the base taboo they require bizarre and alien acts that distance the voice of the void from his own humanity, causing him to take a -1 penalty on Charisma checks and Charisma-based skill checks whenever he accepts a taboo. In return, if the voice of the void is under a blasphemy, the die for his spirit surge changes from 1d6 to 1d8, increasing to 1d10 at 10th level and 1d12 at 20th level. This alters taboo.	SOURCEPAGE:p.212
Void Channeler	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:MediumClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.Supernatural	PRECLASS:1,Medium=3	DESC:At 3rd level, the voice of the void can funnel energy from the emissaries' realm through himself. A number of times per day equal to his Charisma modifier, the medium can unleash a burst of energy that damages all other creatures except aberrations within 30 feet of him. The burst deals 1d6 points of damage + 1d6 additional points of damage for every 2 medium levels the medium has beyond 3rd. Creatures receive a Will save to halve the damage (DC = 10 + 1/2 the medium's level + the medium's Charisma modifier). Creatures with fewer HD than half the medium's level who fail the Will save are also confused for 1d4 rounds. This replaces haunt channeler.	SOURCEPAGE:p.212
Vaultbreaker	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:VillainCodexArchetype.AlchemistArchetype	DESC:Alchemist archetype (Thieves' Guild). Breaking and Entering (1st) replaces the Brew Potion bonus feat. Safecracking (1st) alters bombs and replaces the Throw Anything bonus feat. In place of a discovery, a vaultbreaker can choose the rogue talents expert leaper [APG], fast stealth, ledge walker, nimble climber [APG], or wall scramble [APG] (alters discoveries). Enhanced Safecracking (3rd) alters bombs and replaces the poison use class ability.	SOURCEPAGE:p.236
Breaking and Entering	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:AlchemistClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	PRECLASS:1,Alchemist=1	DESC:A vaultbreaker gains Stealth as a class skill and can disarm magical traps as if he were a rogue with the trapfinding ability. This replaces the Brew Potion bonus feat.	SOURCEPAGE:p.236
Safecracking	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:AlchemistClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	PRECLASS:1,Alchemist=1	DESC:At 1st level, a vaultbreaker's bombs can help him disable locks. He gains penetrating charge (an alchemist discovery) as a bonus discovery. Because this ability replaces Throw Anything, the vaultbreaker's bombs do not add his Intelligence bonus to damage rolls. This alters bombs and replaces the Throw Anything bonus feat.	SOURCEPAGE:p.236
Enhanced Safecracking	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:AlchemistClassFeatures.SpecialQuality.Extraordinary	PRECLASS:1,Alchemist=3	DESC:At 3rd level, a vaultbreaker gains incendiary charge (an alchemist discovery) as a bonus discovery, and his incendiary charges ignore 10 points of an object's hardness instead of 5. This alters bombs and replaces the poison use class ability.	SOURCEPAGE:p.236
